course: dictionary
lesson: 5486
title: Lateral: sideways and clever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lateral is a word about the side. Something that is lateral goes sideways, or lies along the sides of a thing. «The lateral line along a fish's side feels movements in the water.» The line runs along the side of the fish, not along its top or its belly, so lateral means to do with the sides.
explain: Lateral can also describe a clever way of thinking. «Lateral thinking» means solving a problem in a new way instead of the usual step-by-step way. If a puzzle has you stuck, you might try a new route, just as a footballer moves sideways to find a gap in the defence.
explain: Use context to check. Ask yourself: is this about moving sideways, or about the sides of a shape? Or is it about trying a new, clever idea? The words around lateral tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Lateral means to do with the side or sides, or moving sideways.
fact: «Lateral movement» means movement to the side, not forwards or backwards.
fact: «Lateral faces» are the side faces of a prism or pyramid, not the bases.
fact: «Lateral thinking» means solving problems in a new, clever way.
fact: «Lateral reading» means checking a website by opening a new tab and reading what others say about it.
exercise: «The lateral line along a fish's side feels movements in the water.» What does lateral mean in this sentence? | *To do with the side | Hidden deep under the sea | Very fast | Cold and wet
exercise: Ella is stuck on a puzzle. Her teacher says she needs lateral thinking. What does that mean? | Doing the same steps in the same order every time | Giving up quickly | *Finding a new, clever way to solve it | Copying the answer from the back of the book
exercise: In a box shape, which part is a lateral face, not a base? | *A side face of the box | The bottom of the box | The top of the box | The box has no sides
test: Which movement is lateral? | Running straight ahead to the end of the field | *Stepping sideways across the goal | Sliding down a slide | Jumping straight up
test: Fish feel water movement with their lateral line. Where is it? | Inside the mouth | Under the belly | *Along each side of the fish | On the tail only
exam: What does the lateral line of a fish feel? | *Movements in the water | Food on the sea floor | Light and colour | Sound from above
